# Line endings.
#
# Git's default on Windows is to check files out with CRLF. For most of this
# repository that is harmless — Node does not care, and neither does a browser.
#
# For shell scripts it is not harmless at all. A `#!/usr/bin/env bash` script
# with CRLF endings fails on every Linux machine with:
#
#     deploy.sh: line 32: $'\r': command not found
#     set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# — an error that points at the wrong thing entirely and sends people hunting
# through bash options. `deploy.sh` is written to be copied to a server, so it
# has to be LF wherever it lives, including in a Windows working tree.
#
# The same applies to the systemd unit it writes, and to anything else read by
# a Linux tool rather than by Node.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.pdf       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.ico       binary
